22
00:01:27.963 --> 00:01:31.049
<i>My name is Amorowat Anysia Achola.</i>

23
00:01:31.717 --> 00:01:33.135
<i>You can call me Ani.</i>

24
00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:41.143
<i>I'm a senior at Liberty High School.</i>

25
00:01:41.226 --> 00:01:43.061
You were lying to me the whole time.

26
00:01:46.189 --> 00:01:48.900
Goddammit. Ani. I need you!
I need you so fucking bad.

27
00:01:56.908 --> 00:01:57.908
Amorowat?

28
00:02:09.296 --> 00:02:11.048
<i>My mum's a home health care worker.</i>

29
00:02:11.214 --> 00:02:13.842
<i>We just got to Evergreen last spring.
April.</i>

30
00:02:14.092 --> 00:02:15.886
Right. I'm off then.

31
00:02:16.345 --> 00:02:17.345
Wait...

32
00:02:18.889 --> 00:02:20.140
This is fashion?

33
00:02:20.223 --> 00:02:23.101
It is quite stylish. yes. Thank you.

34
00:02:23.435 --> 00:02:26.271
- The things that school allows.
- You don't even know.

35
00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:30.317
I didn't see you all weekend.
I had both days off.

36
00:02:31.109 --> 00:02:33.028
I had projects.

37
00:02:33.695 --> 00:02:36.281
Next Sunday. I'll go to church with you.

38
00:02:36.365 --> 00:02:37.824
- Yes?
- At the very least.

39
00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:07.020
<i>I just started at Liberty in April.</i>

40
00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:09.356
<i>About eight months ago.</i>

41
00:03:10.649 --> 00:03:12.484
<i>Yeah. I'm the new girl.</i>

42
00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:15.946
<i>Do I like Liberty?</i>

43
00:03:17.364 --> 00:03:18.364
<i>Sure.</i>

44
00:03:19.116 --> 00:03:20.826
<i>It's an... interesting place.</i>

45
00:03:23.954 --> 00:03:26.790
<i>Stuff happens at Liberty High School.
you know?</i>

46
00:03:29.543 --> 00:03:32.838
<i>♪ I would like a place I can call my own ♪</i>

47
00:03:33.171 --> 00:03:36.341
<i>♪ Have a conversation on the telephone ♪</i>

48
00:03:36.925 --> 00:03:38.885
<i>I'm guessing that's why I'm here.</i>

49
00:03:40.846 --> 00:03:44.015
<i>♪ I would not complain
Of my wounded heart ♪</i>

50
00:03:44.099 --> 00:03:46.518
<i>You think I know something
about what happened?</i>

51
00:03:50.188 --> 00:03:51.189
Well. I do.

52
00:03:51.857 --> 00:03:54.818
<i>♪ I would like a place
I could call my own ♪</i>

53
00:03:55.485 --> 00:03:58.739
<i>♪ Have a conversation on the telephone ♪</i>

54
00:03:59.156 --> 00:04:01.366
<i>I'm sure you got pieces
from other people.</i>

55
00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:06.288
<i>♪ I would not complain
Of my wounded heart ♪</i>

56
00:04:08.165 --> 00:04:09.958
<i>I can help you put them together.</i>

57
00:04:13.003 --> 00:04:13.837
Jess...

58
00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:16.040
If you're gonna apologize
about the homecoming game...

59
00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:17.089
The police took Clay.

60
00:04:17.841 --> 00:04:20.218
- What?
- Just now. I saw them out front.

61
00:04:20.302 --> 00:04:22.053
Shit! Why now?

62
00:04:22.137 --> 00:04:24.431
It's November.
Spring Fling was last April.

63
00:04:25.724 --> 00:04:26.892
And why Clay?

64
00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:31.271
<i>All units in the vicinity
of Mission and Twelfth.</i>

65
00:04:31.354 --> 00:04:32.354
<i>assault in progress.</i>

66
00:04:32.564 --> 00:04:35.066
<i>1705 Mission. Please respond.</i>

67
00:04:35.525 --> 00:04:36.401
Wanna get that?

68
00:04:36.485 --> 00:04:38.245
- I'll take him back to the station.
- Right.

69
00:04:38.361 --> 00:04:41.448
Dispatch. Unit 12 is responding.
Unit 4 returning to station.

70
00:04:42.449 --> 00:04:44.451
<i>683. that's one. seven. zero...</i>

71
00:05:01.218 --> 00:05:03.470
<i>There are things
I'm sure no one has told you.</i>

72
00:05:04.846 --> 00:05:06.598
<i>Secrets that have been well-kept.</i>

73
00:05:11.645 --> 00:05:15.524
<i>And yes. the keeper of those secrets
is often Clay Jensen.</i>

74
00:05:28.245 --> 00:05:29.246
Do you mind?

75
00:05:33.959 --> 00:05:36.086
<i>One secret goes back to last spring.</i>

76
00:05:39.297 --> 00:05:41.550
- What the hell do you want. Jess?
- The cops took Clay.

77
00:05:41.633 --> 00:05:44.719
They perp-walked him out of school.
Ani saw just now.

78
00:05:44.845 --> 00:05:45.845
Shit!

79
00:05:47.514 --> 00:05:48.807
Do you think they know...

80
00:05:49.349 --> 00:05:50.349
about...

81
00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:52.978
- Tyler?
- Do you think so?

82
00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:55.689
- Did you tell them?
- Are you fucking serious?

83
00:05:55.772 --> 00:05:57.932
- No. of course I didn't tell them.
- Really? 'Cause...

84
00:05:57.983 --> 00:06:00.151
you've been pretty hostile
to everyone lately.

85
00:06:00.235 --> 00:06:02.279
No. I've been pretty hostile
to you lately.

86
00:06:02.946 --> 00:06:05.049
Plus this whole Tyler thing happened
seven months ago.

87
00:06:05.073 --> 00:06:07.784
- Why would I say anything now?
- Why else would they want Clay?

88
00:06:08.535 --> 00:06:11.204
- How would I know?
- Did something happen this weekend?

89
00:06:11.746 --> 00:06:13.874
What did you do
after the homecoming game?

90
00:06:15.041 --> 00:06:16.209
Not very damn much.

91
00:06:19.462 --> 00:06:21.298
- Zach.
- I...

92
00:06:22.299 --> 00:06:23.299
have to go to history.

93
00:06:24.634 --> 00:06:27.095
<i>These kids were connected
by their secrets.</i>

94
00:06:29.472 --> 00:06:31.558
<i>Connected and forever changed.</i>

95
00:06:33.018 --> 00:06:36.688
Here. I'll help you with that.
in terms of ironic things happening.

96
00:06:36.855 --> 00:06:38.732
Not my first time on crutches. Alex.

97
00:06:38.815 --> 00:06:40.525
- C'mon. Zach. give me a win.
- Alex?

98
00:06:42.444 --> 00:06:43.612
The cops were just here.

99
00:06:44.154 --> 00:06:46.031
- They took Clay in.
- Okay.

100
00:06:46.197 --> 00:06:47.741
- Okay?
- Yeah. I mean.

101
00:06:47.824 --> 00:06:49.618
Clay's not gonna say anything
about anybody.

102
00:06:49.701 --> 00:06:51.411
- Jess. come on.
- I have to go.

103
00:06:53.914 --> 00:06:56.750
What's up with her? Hasn't it been
a few months since you guys...

104
00:06:56.833 --> 00:07:00.587
Yeah. I guess it's a quick slide
from "we can be friends"

105
00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:02.130
to "don't fucking touch me."

106
00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:05.300
Your knee seems worse today.

107
00:07:05.717 --> 00:07:08.929
Friday night you could put some weight
on it. right? Without the crutches?

108
00:07:09.054 --> 00:07:10.597
Yeah. I mean...

109
00:07:11.306 --> 00:07:12.724
that's how these things go.

110
00:07:13.642 --> 00:07:14.643
It swells up.

111
00:07:16.978 --> 00:07:18.229
Your eye's looking worse.

112
00:07:18.939 --> 00:07:21.691
Yeah. that's the problem
with fighting football players.

113
00:07:21.775 --> 00:07:24.110
it's like they... they have helmets.

114
00:07:25.612 --> 00:07:28.239
<i>Even the ones
that don't like each other that much.</i>

115
00:07:29.115 --> 00:07:30.116
<i>there's a bond.</i>

116
00:07:30.992 --> 00:07:32.452
<i>They show up for each other.</i>

117
00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:35.413
- Good morning.
- The cops took Clay.

118
00:07:35.830 --> 00:07:37.150
This morning. right outta school.

119
00:07:37.207 --> 00:07:38.208
The sheriffs?

120
00:07:39.542 --> 00:07:41.742
Javi. I gotta take care of something
for an hour or two.

121
00:07:41.795 --> 00:07:43.505
<i>- </i><i>Esta bien.</i>
- You can't go down there.

122
00:07:43.588 --> 00:07:44.589
You got a better idea?

123
00:07:44.673 --> 00:07:47.801
You can't go down there.
It's not a good idea for you. I'll go.

124
00:07:47.884 --> 00:07:49.552
You go down there. That's a better idea.

125
00:07:49.636 --> 00:07:51.906
- What about the guns?
- That's dealt with. You know that.

126
00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:54.265
No. all I know is you and Clay said
you took care of it.

127
00:07:54.349 --> 00:07:55.684
It's best that's all you know.

128
00:08:01.439 --> 00:08:03.566
<i>So. yeah. The story begins
back in April.</i>

129
00:08:04.776 --> 00:08:07.237
<i>I mean. if we're going to understand
how we got here.</i>

130
00:08:10.865 --> 00:08:12.033
I'll be there in two minutes.

131
00:08:12.617 --> 00:08:13.617
I'm free and clear.

132
00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:15.662
I don't even think they looked
as I drove by.

133
00:08:15.745 --> 00:08:18.206
Yeah. Justin and those guys
are gonna talk to the police.

134
00:08:18.289 --> 00:08:19.416
We got a story.

135
00:08:19.541 --> 00:08:22.752
We didn't take it as real.
It's just him. you know?

136
00:08:22.836 --> 00:08:25.422
I heard him talking about it
and I jumped to conclusions.

137
00:08:25.505 --> 00:08:27.549
- It was a total joke. all right?
- Yeah?

138
00:08:27.632 --> 00:08:29.467
It was fucking stupid
but it was a total joke.

139
00:08:29.551 --> 00:08:31.011
- You made a joke?
- I did.

140
00:08:36.307 --> 00:08:37.976
Tyler? How you doing?

141
00:08:39.436 --> 00:08:42.147
Just breathe. man.
Everything's going to be okay.

142
00:08:44.482 --> 00:08:48.528
Wait. they're... They're not coming here.
They're going to the school.

143
00:08:49.362 --> 00:08:52.157
But we need you
to get out of the backpack

144
00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:53.241
and the belt.

145
00:08:54.951 --> 00:08:58.079
I need you to be here... with me.

146
00:09:00.123 --> 00:09:01.916
- No. don't touch me!
- Okay!

147
00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:05.420
- Don't fucking touch me!
- Okay. Tyler! I'm not.

148
00:09:06.046 --> 00:09:07.589
I'm over here. You're good.

149
00:09:08.131 --> 00:09:09.971
But I'm gonna need you
to take off the backpack

150
00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:11.176
and take off the belt

151
00:09:11.259 --> 00:09:12.677
and walk away from them.

152
00:09:27.317 --> 00:09:28.359
Now walk towards me.

153
00:09:32.030 --> 00:09:33.073
It's just Clay.

154
00:09:33.823 --> 00:09:34.949
It's just Clay. see?

155
00:09:35.075 --> 00:09:37.660
I told you we were going to meet up
with him in the car.

156
00:09:38.411 --> 00:09:39.579
Right. Okay.

157
00:09:48.296 --> 00:09:49.296
Hey. Tyler.

158
00:09:49.839 --> 00:09:50.840
How you doing?

159
00:09:51.424 --> 00:09:52.884
Shall we get you home?

160
00:09:56.346 --> 00:09:57.346
Oh. my God...

161
00:09:58.014 --> 00:09:59.014
My parents...

162
00:10:00.350 --> 00:10:01.350
Tyler...

163
00:10:02.727 --> 00:10:03.770
What did you do?

164
00:10:04.896 --> 00:10:07.524
<i>I don't know everything
that's happened since that night.</i>

165
00:10:08.858 --> 00:10:11.736
<i>but I know it was Bryce Walker's
last night at Liberty.</i>

166
00:10:13.613 --> 00:10:15.115
<i>And I'm the new kid. right?</i>

167
00:10:16.241 --> 00:10:18.201
<i>I watch. I listen.</i>

168
00:10:19.369 --> 00:10:20.620
<i>I know quite a bit.</i>

169
00:10:23.414 --> 00:10:25.166
<i>And I'll tell you everything.</i>

170
00:10:28.920 --> 00:10:29.963
Do I need a lawyer?

171
00:10:31.005 --> 00:10:32.715
Oh... No.

172
00:10:34.551 --> 00:10:37.053
No. this isn't any kind
of criminal investigation.

173
00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:39.389
And you're over 18 now. right?

174
00:10:41.516 --> 00:10:42.559
As of last month.

175
00:10:42.642 --> 00:10:44.602
Yeah. so you don't even
need a parent here.

176
00:10:45.145 --> 00:10:47.438
I mean. feel free to call your mom
if you want.

177
00:10:47.981 --> 00:10:49.315
No. Thank you.

178
00:10:49.941 --> 00:10:51.421
So. how are things at Liberty lately?

179
00:10:52.443 --> 00:10:53.528
Fine. I guess.

180
00:10:53.611 --> 00:10:56.656
Pretty stressful though. I imagine.
with everything that's going on.

181
00:10:57.907 --> 00:10:59.868
Hannah's trial. then Bryce.

182
00:11:00.368 --> 00:11:02.620
Then the false alarm
at the dance last spring.

183
00:11:02.704 --> 00:11:04.205
now all this at Homecoming.

184
00:11:04.998 --> 00:11:06.958
More than any one high school deserves.

185
00:11:07.041 --> 00:11:09.711
I think a lot of high schools
go through a lot worse.

186
00:11:09.794 --> 00:11:12.088
You're right.
But this thing with Homecoming...

187
00:11:13.047 --> 00:11:14.047
were you there?

188
00:11:14.465 --> 00:11:16.050
At the game Friday night?

189
00:11:16.426 --> 00:11:17.426
I was.

190
00:11:17.468 --> 00:11:18.720
Did you get caught up in it?

191
00:11:19.304 --> 00:11:21.264
Not so much. A little.

192
00:11:21.681 --> 00:11:23.183
Did you run into Bryce Walker?

193
00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:25.059
We said hello.

194
00:11:25.143 --> 00:11:27.437
Okay. Was this before the game or after?

195
00:11:27.812 --> 00:11:28.812
Before.

196
00:11:30.565 --> 00:11:31.565
Why?

197
00:11:32.525 --> 00:11:33.525
Well...

198
00:11:35.153 --> 00:11:37.530
See. the thing is. Clay...

199
00:11:39.449 --> 00:11:41.826
Bryce was playing for Hillcrest
on Friday night.

200
00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:45.079
He walked off the field
and hasn't been seen since.

201
00:11:48.124 --> 00:11:51.294
Do you have any idea where he could be
or who he could be with?

202
00:11:57.050 --> 00:11:58.051
I don't.

203
00:11:59.385 --> 00:12:00.385
Hmm.

204
00:12:03.389 --> 00:12:04.682
Except for...

205
00:12:07.101 --> 00:12:08.269
we found this...

206
00:12:09.103 --> 00:12:10.605
inside Bryce's room.

207
00:12:11.189 --> 00:12:12.482
You recognize that?

208
00:12:15.902 --> 00:12:17.987
- It used to be mine.
- You have any idea

209
00:12:18.071 --> 00:12:20.740
how Bryce could come to have it
or why would it be in his room?

210
00:12:21.824 --> 00:12:22.659
I don't know.

211
00:12:22.742 --> 00:12:25.370
When's the last time you saw it
or had it in your possession?

212
00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:30.375
I don't remember.
I don't ride a bike anymore.

213
00:12:30.458 --> 00:12:31.458
Okay.

214
00:12:32.877 --> 00:12:33.877
Um...

215
00:12:34.587 --> 00:12:36.756
Clay. you were seen
outside of Bryce's house

216
00:12:36.839 --> 00:12:38.758
a few days before the homecoming game.

217
00:12:39.884 --> 00:12:42.637
You apparently threatened him.

218
00:12:47.684 --> 00:12:49.018
Specifically you said.

219
00:12:49.644 --> 00:12:50.853
"I'll fucking kill you."

220
00:12:52.063 --> 00:12:53.189
Can you explain that?

221
00:12:55.900 --> 00:12:56.818
Who told you that?

222
00:12:56.901 --> 00:12:59.028
It's not important.
Do you remember saying that?

223
00:12:59.946 --> 00:13:02.991
I was... I was checking on a friend.

224
00:13:03.616 --> 00:13:04.659
their safety.

225
00:13:04.742 --> 00:13:07.203
I mean. Bryce has a history.

226
00:13:10.498 --> 00:13:12.667
A triangle...

227
00:13:13.042 --> 00:13:14.919
by repeatedly removing

228
00:13:15.003 --> 00:13:17.964
the middle triangle
from each of the prior generations.

229
00:13:18.506 --> 00:13:21.426
the number of colored triangles increases

230
00:13:21.509 --> 00:13:22.844
by a factor of...?

231
00:13:23.928 --> 00:13:27.265
Triangle recursion by a factor of three.

232
00:13:27.932 --> 00:13:29.058
- Mr. Wood?
- Yes?

233
00:13:29.309 --> 00:13:32.603
Would it be possible for me to run
to the robotics room for a few?

234
00:13:32.687 --> 00:13:35.565
I've just realized
I've left a battery overcharging

235
00:13:35.648 --> 00:13:37.442
and it's going to fry the motherboard.

236
00:13:37.525 --> 00:13:40.361
Not a problem. I doubt
you need this review in the first place.

237
00:13:40.445 --> 00:13:43.114
Well. I wasn't going to say anything.
but thank you.

238
00:13:46.451 --> 00:13:48.828
Is there anything else
you think I should know?

239
00:13:51.247 --> 00:13:52.248
No.

240
00:13:58.171 --> 00:14:00.423
All right.
I got to go check on a few things.

241
00:14:01.215 --> 00:14:02.675
Be back in a couple of minutes.

242
00:14:02.759 --> 00:14:04.427
Feel free to use your cell phone.

243
00:14:37.919 --> 00:14:39.545
Clay. my name is Nora Walker.

244
00:14:41.047 --> 00:14:43.007
Yes. I know... I know who you are.

245
00:14:52.725 --> 00:14:56.354
Clay. I know Bryce hurt you
and friends of yours.

246
00:14:57.355 --> 00:14:59.190
He's done some monstrous things.

247
00:15:02.193 --> 00:15:03.236
But he's my son.

248
00:15:04.529 --> 00:15:08.074
